      "content": "First and foremost, ensure your entire team is wearing appropriate protective gear, including gloves and safety goggles. Do not attempt to open the battery further or puncture it, as this can be highly dangerous. Carefully place the phone into a secure plastic bag to prevent any potential fire hazards. You should send the smartphone, along with the damaged battery, to a certified e-waste recycler. Do not dispose of it through conventional waste channels. Provide proper documentation and labeling for the e-waste facility to handle it appropriately.",
